 "short": "Nonhomogeneous equations",
 "lead": "A linear equation whose right-hand side is not zero, such as the equation of a forced vibration, is solved in two pieces: the <span data-concept=\"general-solution\">general solution</span> of the homogeneous equation it comes from, and any one <span data-concept=\"particular-solution\">particular solution</span> of the equation itself. This section shows why the two pieces are enough, how to guess the one solution when the right-hand side is a polynomial, an exponential or a sine, and what to do when no guess works.",
